In expo-app/App.tsx (line 35) the arrow function used for `tabBarButton` has an untyped `props` parameter, causing a TypeScript error (TS7006: Parameter 'props' implicitly has an 'any' type). Add an explicit type annotation, e.g.:
```tsx
import { BottomTabBarButtonProps } from '@react-navigation/bottom-tabs';
// ...
 tabBarButton: (props: BottomTabBarButtonProps) => {
   const { onPress, accessibilityState, accessibilityLabel, style, children } = props;
   // ...
 }
``` 
This will resolve the `tsc` failure.

- In expo-app/src/screens/MileageEntryScreen.tsx the Date `<TextInput>` is not reliably discoverable by the automated UI flow (step 25 “fill field 'Date'” times out). Add an explicit accessibility role (and ensure the label is set) so Playwright can locate it, e.g.:
```tsx
<TextInput
  placeholder="Date"
  value={date}
  onChangeText={setDate}
  style={styles.input}
  accessibilityLabel="Date"
  accessibilityRole="textbox"
/>
```
(Apply the same fix to the Date field in ReceiptCaptureScreen.tsx if desired.) This will allow the UI primary‑flow test to fill the Date field successfully.
